  "body": "I'm seeing something really wonky in the spec. A number of [table elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/tables.html#the-tr-element) have a big loud box saying:\n\n> This feature is in the process of being removed from the Web platform. (This is a long process that takes many years.) Using this element at this time is highly discouraged.\n\n![image](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/129203/14223346/07dfcaa4-f84c-11e5-9652-90acd5cc1fc4.png)\n\nThis was news to me, so I searched to see if it's possible I'm really that out of touch with HTML and didn't come up with anything. That combined with other things makes me think this is just some weird error? In the multipage version it says it for `tbody|thead|tr|td`. In the single page version it says it for `table|tfoot|th`. In other words, they're inverses.\n\n(Also, why can't the content of those boxes be selected or found via the browser's search?)\n",
